<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wolfgang, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1492–1566</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wolfgang was Prince of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kothen">Köthen</a> and one of the first German princes to adopt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. In 1530 he signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg-confession">Augsburg Confession</a>, and he joined the Protestant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-league">Schmalkaldic League</a>. After the league's defeat at Mühlberg in 1547 Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> placed him under the imperial ban and took his lands, but he recovered them in 1552. Childless, he later handed his principality to his relatives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wolfgang-prince-of-anhalt-kothen.jpg" alt="Wolfgang, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meister I.S. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WolfgangvonAnhalt.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
